      {
        "id": "p82-task29-34-part-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{x+2}<2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-2$ or $x>-\\dfrac32$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-2$, $(x+2)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+2&<2(x+2)^2\\\\2(x+2)^2-(x+2)&>0\\\\(x+2)(2x+3)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is positive outside its zeroes. Thus $x<-2$ or $x>-\\dfrac32$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task29-34-part-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2}{x-1}>4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1<x<\\dfrac32$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne1$, $(x-1)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(x-1)&>4(x-1)^2\\\\4(x-1)^2-2(x-1)&<0\\\\2(x-1)(2x-3)&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is negative between its zeroes. Thus $1<x<\\dfrac32$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task29-34-part-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x}{x+4}<3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-6$ or $x>-4$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-4$, $(x+4)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x+4)&<3(x+4)^2\\\\3(x+4)^2-x(x+4)&>0\\\\2(x+4)(x+6)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is positive outside its zeroes. Thus $x<-6$ or $x>-4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task29-34-part-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x}{x-2}>1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-2$ or $x>2$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne2$, $(x-2)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x(x-2)&>(x-2)^2\\\\2x(x-2)-(x-2)^2&>0\\\\(x-2)(x+2)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is positive outside its zeroes. Thus $x<-2$ or $x>2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task29-34-part-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x-3}{x+1}>2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-5<x<-1$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-1$, $(x+1)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-3)(x+1)&>2(x+1)^2\\\\2(x+1)^2-(x-3)(x+1)&<0\\\\(x+1)(x+5)&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is negative between its zeroes. Thus $-5<x<-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task29-34-part-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3-x}{x+4}<1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-4$ or $x>-\\dfrac12$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-4$, $(x+4)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}(3-x)(x+4)&<(x+4)^2\\\\(x+4)^2-(3-x)(x+4)&>0\\\\(x+4)(2x+1)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is positive outside its zeroes. Thus $x<-4$ or $x>-\\dfrac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
    ]
  },
